{"id":"lois-red-tape","title":"Red Tape and White Knuckles","who":"Lois Pryce","when":"2006","vehicle":"Yamaha XT225","kind":"moto","color":"#be185d","media":[{"kind":"book","title":"Lois on the Loose","by":"Lois Pryce"},{"kind":"book","title":"Red Tape and White Knuckles","by":"Lois Pryce"},{"kind":"book","title":"Revolutionary Ride","by":"Lois Pryce","note":"Her solo rides in Iran, 2013–14"}],"summary":"Lois Pryce rides alone from her London home to Cape Town: across the Sahara through Algeria and Niger, down West Africa, through the Congo basin's jungle tracks and the minefields of post-war Angola, about 10,000 miles in four months. The book tells it with humour, and plenty of border bureaucracy.","sources":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Lois Pryce","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lois_Pryce"},{"label":"ONE: meet Lois, who rode from London to Cape Town","url":"https://www.one.org/stories/meet-lois-the-woman-who-travelled-from-london-to-cape-town-by-motorbike"}],"approximate":"The countries named in accounts of the book; the towns and roads are approximate.","km":13313,"bbox":[-0.1278,-33.9287,18.9899,51.5074],"stops":[{"name":"London","place":"London, UK","at":[51.5074,-0.1278],"text":"The start from home."},{"name":"Tunisia","place":"Tunis, Tunisia","at":[36.8002,10.1858],"text":"Across the Mediterranean to Africa.","by":"ferry"},{"name":"Algeria (Sahara)","place":"Tamanrasset, Algeria","at":[22.7859,5.5291],"text":"South across the Algerian Sahara."},{"name":"Niger","place":"Agadez, Niger","at":[16.9726,7.9907],"text":"Out of the desert into Niger."},{"name":"Nigeria","place":"Kano, Nigeria","at":[11.994,8.522],"text":"Into Nigeria."},{"name":"Cameroon","place":"Yaoundé, Cameroon","at":[3.869,11.5213],"text":"Down into Cameroon."},{"name":"Gabon","place":"Libreville, Gabon","at":[0.4087,9.4419],"text":"Gabon's forests."},{"name":"Congo","place":"Pointe-Noire, Republic of the Congo","at":[-4.7975,11.8503],"text":"The Congo basin: mud, jungle and checkpoints."},{"nam